# Title: File Encryption/Decryption Via Gpg4win From Suspicious Locations
# ID: e1e0b7d7-e10b-4ee4-ac49-a4bda05d320d
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), X__Junior (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2022-11-30
# Tags: attack.execution
# Description: Detects usage of Gpg4win to encrypt/decrypt files located in potentially suspicious locations.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((CommandLine CONTAIN "-passphrase") AND (((Image="*\\gpg.exe" OR Image="*\\gpg2.exe")) OR (Product = "GNU Privacy Guard (GnuPG)") OR (Description = "GnuPG’s OpenPGP tool")) AND ((CommandLine CONTAIN ":\\PerfLogs\\" OR CommandLine CONTAIN ":\\Temp\\" OR CommandLine CONTAIN ":\\Users\\Public\\" OR CommandLine CONTAIN ":\\Windows\\Temp\\" OR CommandLine CONTAIN "\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\" OR CommandLine CONTAIN "\\AppData\\Roaming\\")))
